1) Tests\Feature\ConfigContractTest::test_decimal_precision_is_two_not_whole_dirhams
NEARS-2019 (EXPECTED RED — the money defect, not a broken build): digit_after_decimal_point is not 2, so PlaceNewOrder rounds PERSISTED order money to whole dirhams — order_amount, delivery_charge, total_tax_amount, the discount fields and every order_details line price. Up to a half-dirham is added to or removed from what the customer is actually charged. THIS TEST READS THE PHPUNIT TWIN (multi_food_db_test*), NEVER multi_food_db, so it pins the SEED contract and not the live config. CORRECTING THE LIVE SETTING ALONE WILL NOT CLEAR IT — a data change never triggers a re-clone (setup_test_db.sh re-clones only on an applied-migration-signature mismatch). To go green, all three: (1) set digit_after_decimal_point to 2 via Admin -> Business Setup or a versioned seeder, never raw DML, then `php artisan cache:clear` (settings are cached rememberForever, so skipping this makes a correct fix look like it failed); (2) re-dump the corrected DB and rebuild the twin: TEST_DB_BACKUP=/path/to/dump.sql bash scripts/setup_test_db.sh ; (3) FORCE the clones to rebuild: bash scripts/setup_test_db.sh --drop-stale (or --clone <worktree_slug> per worktree). See docs/solutions/NEARS-2019-persisted-money-rounding.md.
